derivations.claim:
Set $X_0:=X$. As long as $X_{i-1}
eq\varnothing$, choose a vertex $v_i\in X_{i-1}$ of maximum degree in $G[X_{i-1}]$, let $A_i:=N_{G[X_{i-1}]}(v_i)$, choose a stable set $C_i\subseteq A_i$ with $|C_i|\geq |A_i|^	au/\omega(G)$, and let $X_i$ be the set of vertices in $X_{i-1}\setminus\{v_i\}$ with no neighbour in $\{v_i\}\cup C_i$. This is possible because when $A_i
eq\varnothing$, the induced subgraph $G[A_i]$ is proper, so [L1] and [L2] give $\alpha(G[A_i])\geq \kappa(G[A_i])/\omega(G)\geq |A_i|^	au/\omega(G)$. The process stops after finitely many steps because $v_i
otin X_i$, so $|X_i|<|X_{i-1}|$ whenever $X_{i-1}
eq\varnothing$.
